DevOps Capability Assessment Project
1. Executive Elevator Pitch
TP Orion is an AI-assisted DevOps capability assessment platform that guides enterprise teams through a structured maturity evaluation. A React front-end orchestrates the interview-style workflow, while a FastAPI backend pairs deterministic scoring with Azure OpenAI reasoning to generate follow-up probes, sufficiency checks, and tailored remediation roadmaps. Assessment state, generated reports, and secrets are managed with Azure-native services, enabling repeatable, compliant advisory engagements.

Your talking points
"I delivered an end-to-end assessment experience where the UI, API, and Azure services stay in sync around a single user session ID."
"I engineered guardrails like skip thresholds and sufficiency validation so AI suggestions remain grounded in the collected evidence."
"I automated post-assessment assets (PDF/HTML exports, recommendation bundles) to jump-start stakeholder conversations."
2. System Architecture At A Glance
Layer	Tech	Responsibilities
Front-end	React 18 + Vite	Session bootstrap, question navigation, skip tracking, follow-up capture, surfacing category/overall recommendations, download actions
API	FastAPI, Pydantic	State management APIs, LLM orchestration, scoring, skip enforcement, recommendation aggregation, asset generation
AI & Data	Azure OpenAI, Azure SQL, Azure Blob Storage, Azure Key Vault	Prompted reasoning, question catalog, answer persistence, state blobs, report storage, secret governance
Key integration points:

All UI calls use a generated user_id (/session/start). That ID ties SQL answer rows, blob state, and report files together.
Azure Key Vault supplies secrets for SQL, OpenAI, and Blob Storage, injected at runtime by AzureKeyVaultManager.
Follow-up workflows call Azure OpenAI with chunked prompts (chunk_summary_for_llm) to respect token limits.
3. Backend Walkthrough (FastAPI)
Session & State Services
POST /session/start creates a GUID used across the assessment.
State blobs are stored per user in Azure Blob (assessment_state_<user>.json) managed by AzureBlobStateManager.
Question Flow
GET /categories composes category completion status by combining SQL catalog entries with stored answers and follow-ups.
GET /questions/next streams unanswered baseline questions per category.
POST /answers/submit persists answers to Azure SQL via QuestionsDB and mirrors them in the blob state. It recalculates completion, logging debug insights for observability.
Sufficiency, Follow-ups, and Recommendations
POST /assessment/check_and_followups:
Builds a category summary (build_assessment_summary_for_category).
Enforces skip limit (>=40% unanswered) before LLM calls.
Invokes Azure OpenAI to judge sufficiency; if lacking, generates follow-up questions using call_llm_for_follow_ups_category with deduping against historical follow-ups.
Computes category scoring metrics (initial vs follow-up) for the UI.
POST /assessment/recommendations (see call_llm_for_recommendations_only) synthesizes action plans once sufficiency is achieved.
generate_and_store_report converts final insights into HTML/PDF, uploads to Blob Storage, and returns shareable URLs.
Supporting Utilities
calculate_scores and build_assessment_summary compute maturity percentages for each domain.
chunk_summary_for_llm splits long payloads to protect against token overflow in Azure OpenAI calls.
Logging is centralized via devops_agent.log and api_debug.log for operational telemetry.
Azure Dependencies
Azure SQL (QuestionsDB): serves question catalog, follow-up storage, and captured answers.
Azure Blob Storage: session state, generated reports, and follow-up artifacts.
Azure Key Vault: rotated secrets for all credentials (kv_manager.get_secret).
Azure OpenAI: conversation, sufficiency validation, follow-up generation, recommendation authoring.
4. Front-end Walkthrough (React + Vite)
Application Shell (App.jsx)
Bootstraps a user session by calling /session/start and stores the returned userId.
Loads category completion data, highlights resets, and enforces a skip ceiling (40%) with banner messaging.
Governs a dual-track questionnaire: baseline questions followed by LLM-generated follow-ups.
Tracks answer counts, skip counts, and sufficiency flags to time backend calls.
Surfaces AI progress copy (AI_INITIAL_MESSAGES, AI_RECHECK_MESSAGES) during long-running checks.
Question Capture (QuestionForm.jsx)
Renders dynamic controls (radio, checkbox, slider, text) based on question metadata from the API.
Sends answers through the handleAnswer callback, which maps to /answers/submit.
Recommendations (Recommendations.jsx, AllRecommendations.jsx)
Displays category-specific and overall recommendations once sufficiency is met.
Integrates with custom hooks (useCategoryRecommendations, useOverallRecommendations) that lazily fetch LLM outputs and scores.
UI Enhancements
BackgroundOverlay adds brand-consistent gradients.
Modals (Overall & Category) show scorecards and allow download of export bundles.
CTA buttons connect to the teaser landing page assets you built (orion-release-teaser.html) including Launch TP ORION and Sample Report download.
5. Data & AI Lifecycle
Question Catalog: Stored in Azure SQL with categories, baseline questions, and potential follow-ups (is_follow_up).
Answer Ingestion: /answers/submit writes each response, optional comments, and whether it was follow-up driven.
Skip Monitoring: Blob state tracks unanswered ratio; passing 40% triggers a hard stop in the backend and a reset in the UI.
Sufficiency Evaluation: Azure OpenAI reviews category summaries; insufficiency triggers contextual follow-ups.
Recommendation Generation: Once sufficient, call_llm_for_recommendations_only produces actionable steps, stored and exposed to the UI.
Report Packaging: generate_and_store_report assembles HTML/PDF artifacts, uploads to Blob, and returns secure URLs for stakeholders.
6. Operational Considerations
Security: No secrets hard-coded; Key Vault retrieval happens at startup. CORS is fully open for now—mention tightening origins for production.
Observability: Extensive print and logging.debug outputs document category stats, sufficiency results, and follow-up dedupe decisions. Consider log aggregation (App Insights) as a next step.
Scalability: FastAPI endpoints are stateless; horizontal scale depends on Blob + SQL throughput. AI calls are the dominant latency—chunking and async improvements are possible.
Error Handling: Exceptions bubble as HTTP 400/500 responses; UI monitors res.ok and communicates via banners/modals.
